Title: E-Commerce Platform
Slug: (auto-fills)
Short Description: A full-featured online store built with Django templates and PostgreSQL.

The Problem:
"Small businesses in my area had no online presence. They were losing customers
to larger competitors who had e-commerce capabilities. I wanted to build a
solution that was affordable and easy for non-technical owners to manage."

The Solution:
"Built a complete e-commerce platform with Django templates. The system handles
product listings, cart management, user authentication, and order processing.
Used Django's class-based views for clean, maintainable code and implemented
custom template tags for reusable UI components."

Architecture Decision:
"Chose Django Templates over a JavaScript framework because the client needed
SEO-friendly pages and fast initial load times. Django's template inheritance
allowed me to create a consistent layout while keeping the code DRY. Used
WhiteNoise for static file serving to simplify deployment."

Lessons Learned:
"This project taught me the importance of proper model design. Initially, I
designed the Product and Order models poorly, which led to complex queries.
After refactoring to use foreign keys properly and adding database indexes,
page load times improved by 60%. I also learned to use Django's select_related
and prefetch_related to avoid the N+1 query problem."

Tech Stack: Django, Django Templates, PostgreSQL, WhiteNoise, Bootstrap, Stripe

